# 710 - Custom Class Resource Bars

## Status
- Created: 2026-04-05
- Phase: 2
- Priority: Medium
- Depends on: 345 (custom talent interface), 159 (knight custom class)

## Current Behavior
- Each WoW class has fixed resource types (mana, rage, energy, runic power, combo points, runes)
- Resource type is determined by class in DBC files
- Custom classes use their base class's resource only
- Spells requiring other resources (e.g., Sprint needs energy) cannot be cast by other classes

## Intended Behavior
- Custom classes automatically gain resource bars based on their spell sources
- If a custom class has ANY spell from a source class, they gain that class's resources
- Extra resources displayed as floating bars (AIO)
- Base class resource stays in default position
- Resources behave identically to how they work for the source class

## Resource Types

| Resource | Source Classes | Max | Regeneration |
|----------|---------------|-----|--------------|
| Mana | Most casters, Paladin, Hunter | Varies | 5% base mana/5sec (Spirit scaling) |
| Rage | Warrior, Bear | 100 | Generated by damage dealt/taken |
| Energy | Rogue, Cat | 100 | 10/sec base |
| Runic Power | Death Knight | 100 | Generated by rune abilities |
| Combo Points | Rogue, Cat | 5 | Generated by combo builders |
| Runes | Death Knight | 6 | 10sec cooldown per rune |

## Automatic Resource Detection

Resources are determined by examining the custom class's spell sources:

```lua
-- {{{ detectRequiredResources
-- Scans custom class definition and returns required resource types
function CustomClasses.detectRequiredResources(definition)
    local resources = {}
    local sourceClasses = {}

    -- Collect all source classes
    for _, spell in ipairs(definition.spells) do
        sourceClasses[spell.sourceClass] = true
    end

    -- Map source classes to resources
    local classResources = {
        [1] = { "rage" },           -- Warrior
        [2] = { "mana" },           -- Paladin
        [3] = { "mana" },           -- Hunter (WotLK)
        [4] = { "energy", "combo" }, -- Rogue
        [5] = { "mana" },           -- Priest
        [6] = { "runic", "runes" }, -- Death Knight
        [7] = { "mana" },           -- Shaman
        [8] = { "mana" },           -- Mage
        [9] = { "mana" },           -- Warlock
        [11] = { "mana" },          -- Druid (base form)
    }

    for sourceClass, _ in pairs(sourceClasses) do
        local classRes = classResources[sourceClass]
        if classRes then
            for _, res in ipairs(classRes) do
                resources[res] = true
            end
        end
    end

    return resources
end -- }}}
```

## Knight Example

Knight sources: Paladin, Priest, Rogue, Warrior, Death Knight, Mage, Hunter

| Source | Resources Gained |
|--------|------------------|
| Paladin (base) | Mana (default bar) |
| Priest | Mana (already have) |
| Rogue | Energy, Combo Points |
| Warrior | Rage |
| Death Knight | Runic Power, Runes |
| Mage | Mana (already have) |
| Hunter | Mana (already have) |

**Knight has:** Mana (default), Energy, Combo Points, Rage, Runic Power, Runes

**Current Knight spells that use these:**
- Sprint: 40 Energy
- (If Riposte was kept): 10 Energy, +1 Combo Point
- Horn of Winter: Generates Runic Power

Note: Having unused resources is fine. Knight generates combo points but has no finishers - that's okay, they just accumulate uselessly.

## Visual Design

### Default Resource Bar
- Base class resource (e.g., Mana for Paladin-based Knight) stays in normal position
- Uses default WoW UI, no modification needed

### Extra Resource Bars (AIO)
- Floating bars for non-base-class resources
- Match WoW's default textures and colors per resource type:
  - Energy: Yellow bar
  - Rage: Red bar
  - Runic Power: Light blue bar
  - Combo Points: 5 red/yellow dots

### Runes (if needed)
- 6 rune display matching DK default
- Blood (red), Frost (blue), Unholy (green)
- Show cooldown state

### Bar Behavior
- **Move:** Ctrl + Left-click drag
- **Resize:** Ctrl + Right-click drag
- **Hide:** Options menu toggle per resource type
- **Reset position:** Options menu button

### Position Persistence
- Bar positions saved per character
- Stored in SavedVariables (client-side)
- Or character_custom_ui table (server-side via AIO)

## Server-Side Implementation (ALE Lua)

### Resource Tracking
```lua
-- Per-player resource storage
local PlayerResources = {}

-- {{{ initPlayerResources
function CustomClasses.initPlayerResources(player)
    local guid = player:GetGUIDLow()
    local customClassId = CustomClasses.getCustomClass(player)

    if not customClassId then return end

    local def = CustomClasses.getDefinition(customClassId)
    local required = CustomClasses.detectRequiredResources(def)

    PlayerResources[guid] = {}

    if required.energy then
        PlayerResources[guid].energy = { current = 100, max = 100 }
    end
    if required.rage then
        PlayerResources[guid].rage = { current = 0, max = 100 }
    end
    if required.runic then
        PlayerResources[guid].runicPower = { current = 0, max = 100 }
    end
    if required.combo then
        PlayerResources[guid].comboPoints = { current = 0, max = 5 }
    end
    if required.runes then
        PlayerResources[guid].runes = {
            { type = "blood", ready = true, cooldown = 0 },
            { type = "blood", ready = true, cooldown = 0 },
            { type = "frost", ready = true, cooldown = 0 },
            { type = "frost", ready = true, cooldown = 0 },
            { type = "unholy", ready = true, cooldown = 0 },
            { type = "unholy", ready = true, cooldown = 0 },
        }
    end
end -- }}}
```

### Resource Regeneration
```lua
-- {{{ updateEnergyRegen
-- Called every 100ms for energy regeneration
function CustomClasses.updateEnergyRegen(player)
    local guid = player:GetGUIDLow()
    local res = PlayerResources[guid]
    if not res or not res.energy then return end

    -- 10 energy per second = 1 energy per 100ms
    res.energy.current = math.min(res.energy.max, res.energy.current + 1)

    -- Notify client
    AIO.Msg():Add("CustomResources", "Update", "energy", res.energy.current):Send(player)
end -- }}}
```

### Spell Cast Interception
```lua
-- {{{ onSpellCast
-- Hook spell cast to check custom resource requirements
-- Note: We read requirements from spell data, not config
RegisterPlayerEvent(PLAYER_EVENT_ON_CAST_SPELL, function(event, player, spell, skipCheck)
    if skipCheck then return end

    local guid = player:GetGUIDLow()
    local res = PlayerResources[guid]
    if not res then return end  -- Not a custom class

    local spellId = spell:GetEntry()
    local cost = GetSpellResourceCost(spellId)  -- Read from spell data

    -- Check energy
    if cost.energy and cost.energy > 0 then
        if not res.energy or res.energy.current < cost.energy then
            player:SendEquipError(142, nil, nil)  -- "Not enough energy"
            return false  -- Cancel cast
        end
    end

    -- Check other resources similarly...
end)

-- {{{ onSpellCastSuccess
-- Consume resources after successful cast
RegisterPlayerEvent(PLAYER_EVENT_ON_CAST_SPELL_FINISH, function(event, player, spell)
    local guid = player:GetGUIDLow()
    local res = PlayerResources[guid]
    if not res then return end

    local spellId = spell:GetEntry()
    local cost = GetSpellResourceCost(spellId)

    -- Consume energy
    if cost.energy and res.energy then
        res.energy.current = res.energy.current - cost.energy
        AIO.Msg():Add("CustomResources", "Update", "energy", res.energy.current):Send(player)
    end

    -- Generate combo points
    if cost.generatesCombo and res.comboPoints then
        res.comboPoints.current = math.min(5, res.comboPoints.current + 1)
        AIO.Msg():Add("CustomResources", "Update", "combo", res.comboPoints.current):Send(player)
    end
end)
```

## Client-Side Implementation (AIO Addon)

### Frame Creation
```lua
-- {{{ CreateResourceBar
local function CreateResourceBar(resourceType, color)
    local bar = CreateFrame("StatusBar", "CustomResource_" .. resourceType, UIParent)
    bar:SetSize(150, 20)
    bar:SetPoint("CENTER", UIParent, "CENTER", 0, -100)
    bar:SetStatusBarTexture("Interface\\TargetingFrame\\UI-StatusBar")
    bar:SetStatusBarColor(unpack(color))
    bar:SetMinMaxValues(0, 100)
    bar:SetValue(100)

    -- Background
    bar.bg = bar:CreateTexture(nil, "BACKGROUND")
    bar.bg:SetAllPoints()
    bar.bg:SetColorTexture(0, 0, 0, 0.5)

    -- Text
    bar.text = bar:CreateFontString(nil, "OVERLAY", "GameFontNormal")
    bar.text:SetPoint("CENTER")
    bar.text:SetText("100/100")

    -- Make moveable
    bar:SetMovable(true)
    bar:EnableMouse(true)
    bar:SetScript("OnMouseDown", function(self, button)
        if IsControlKeyDown() and button == "LeftButton" then
            self:StartMoving()
        end
    end)
    bar:SetScript("OnMouseUp", function(self)
        self:StopMovingOrSizing()
        SaveBarPosition(resourceType, self:GetPoint())
    end)

    return bar
end -- }}}

-- Resource colors matching WoW defaults
local RESOURCE_COLORS = {
    energy = { 1, 1, 0 },      -- Yellow
    rage = { 1, 0, 0 },        -- Red
    runicPower = { 0, 0.82, 1 }, -- Light blue
}
```

### Combo Points Display
```lua
-- {{{ CreateComboPoints
local function CreateComboPoints()
    local frame = CreateFrame("Frame", "CustomResource_Combo", UIParent)
    frame:SetSize(100, 20)
    frame:SetPoint("CENTER", UIParent, "CENTER", 0, -130)

    frame.points = {}
    for i = 1, 5 do
        local dot = frame:CreateTexture(nil, "ARTWORK")
        dot:SetSize(15, 15)
        dot:SetPoint("LEFT", frame, "LEFT", (i-1) * 20, 0)
        dot:SetTexture("Interface\\ComboFrame\\ComboPoint")
        dot:SetVertexColor(1, 0.5, 0, 0.3)  -- Dim when empty
        frame.points[i] = dot
    end

    return frame
end

local function UpdateComboPoints(count)
    for i = 1, 5 do
        if i <= count then
            ComboFrame.points[i]:SetVertexColor(1, 0.5, 0, 1)  -- Bright
        else
            ComboFrame.points[i]:SetVertexColor(1, 0.5, 0, 0.3)  -- Dim
        end
    end
end -- }}}
```

### AIO Message Handler
```lua
local CustomResources = AIO.AddHandlers("CustomResources", {})

function CustomResources.Init(player, resources)
    -- Create bars for each resource the player has
    for resType, data in pairs(resources) do
        if resType == "combo" then
            CreateComboPoints()
        else
            CreateResourceBar(resType, RESOURCE_COLORS[resType])
        end
    end
end

function CustomResources.Update(player, resType, value)
    -- Update the appropriate bar
    local bar = _G["CustomResource_" .. resType]
    if bar then
        bar:SetValue(value)
        bar.text:SetText(value .. "/" .. bar.max)
    end
end
```

## Edge Cases

### Logout/Login
- Save current resource values to `character_custom_resources` table
- Restore on login
- Match default behavior: mana persists, energy/rage reset

### Death/Resurrection
- Match default behavior:
  - Mana: Restored based on res spell
  - Energy: Full on res
  - Rage: 0 on res
  - Runic Power: 0 on res
  - Combo Points: 0 on res

### Shapeshift Forms
- If custom class can shapeshift (Druid spells):
  - Cat form: Use energy bar (hide others)
  - Bear form: Use rage bar (hide others)
  - Caster form: Use mana bar + extra floating bars

### Combat Log
- Resource gains/losses shown in standard format:
  - "You gain 10 Energy"
  - "You lose 40 Energy"
  - "You gain 1 Combo Point"
- Use `SendAddonMessage` or combat log injection if possible

## Database Schema

```sql
-- Resource bar positions per character (optional, can use SavedVariables instead)
CREATE TABLE character_custom_resource_ui (
    guid INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
    resource_type VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
    pos_x FLOAT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    pos_y FLOAT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    width FLOAT NOT NULL DEFAULT 150,
    height FLOAT NOT NULL DEFAULT 20,
    visible TINYINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    PRIMARY KEY (guid, resource_type)
);

-- Current resource values (for persistence across logout)
CREATE TABLE character_custom_resources (
    guid INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,
    resource_type VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
    current_value INT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    PRIMARY KEY (guid, resource_type)
);
```

